diff --git a/docs/en/win32-letterbox.md b/docs/en/win32-letterbox.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8b2ffe9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/en/win32-letterbox.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Win32 letterbox cropping
+
+Enable **Crop top and bottom bars to fit the standard aspect ratio** in Settings → Connection settings. It defaults to off, is saved per instance, and is disabled while tasks run. Reconnect after changing.
+
+The controller removes symmetric top/bottom bars before normal scaling and adds the crop offset back to input coordinates. Dimensions are calculated: 2560×1600 → 2560×1440 (80 pixels per bar), 1920×1200 → 1920×1080 (60), and 1280×800 → 1280×720 (40).
+
+16:9 or wider captures pass through. Taller captures require width divisible by 16 and equal integer bars. Each band is sampled every four pixels; 99.5% of samples must have RGB channels at most 16. Invalid captures or client-size changes block positional input until a valid capture; releases remain available. Side bars and layouts that change with aspect ratio are unsupported.
+
+Uses the public custom-controller API around the original Win32 controller; no native DLL changes. The inner controller uses raw dimensions and the outer controller applies normal scaling. Win32-specific options absent from the custom API are unsupported.
+
+All 11 tests pass with native 5.12.3 and 5.14.2. A MaaKes user confirmed the coffee task at 2560×1600; other dimensions have synthetic coverage only. Test project: `MFAAvalonia.Letterbox.Tests`.
